      "question": "Use the binomial series to expand 1/(2 + 5x)^3, valid for |x| < 2/5, in ascending powers of x up to and including the term in x^3. Give each coefficient as a fraction in its simplest form.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "1/(2 + 5x)^3 = 1/8 - 15x/16 + 75x^2/16 - 625x^3/32 + ...",
      "steps": [
        "Take out the constant: (2 + 5x)^(-3) = 2^(-3)(1 + 5x/2)^(-3) = (1/8)(1 + 5x/2)^(-3).",
        "Use (1 + y)^(-3) = 1 - 3y + 6y^2 - 10y^3 + ..., with y = 5x/2.",
        "Substitute: 1 - 15x/2 + 75x^2/2 - 625x^3/4 + ...",
        "Multiply by 1/8: 1/8 - 15x/16 + 75x^2/16 - 625x^3/32."
      ],
      "images": [
