      "question": "Use the binomial expansion to expand (4 - 5x)^(-1/2), |x| < 4/5, in ascending powers of x up to and including the term in x^2, giving each coefficient as a fully simplified fraction.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "(4 - 5x)^(-1/2) = 1/2 + 5x/16 + 75x^2/256 + ...",
      "steps": [
        "Write (4 - 5x)^(-1/2) = 4^(-1/2)(1 - 5x/4)^(-1/2) = (1/2)(1 - 5x/4)^(-1/2).",
        "Use (1 - y)^(-1/2) = 1 + y/2 + 3y^2/8 + ..., with y = 5x/4.",
        "Substitute: 1 + 5x/8 + (3/8)(25x^2/16) = 1 + 5x/8 + 75x^2/128.",
        "Multiply by 1/2: 1/2 + 5x/16 + 75x^2/256."
