      "question": "f(x) = (2 + kx)/sqrt(4 - 5x), where k is a constant and |x| < 4/5. The series expansion of f(x) in ascending powers of x is 1 + (3/10)x + mx^2 + ... Find the value of k.",
      "status": "ready",
      "answer": "k = -13/20.",
      "steps": [
        "From part (a), 1/sqrt(4 - 5x) = 1/2 + 5x/16 + 75x^2/256 + ...",
        "Multiply by (2 + kx): the x term is 2(5/16) + k(1/2) = 5/8 + k/2.",
        "Set equal to 3/10: k/2 = 3/10 - 5/8 = -13/40.",
        "So k = -13/20."
      ],
